# What the study of the origin and definitions of ice, water and gas found (study/r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin.md). The proposal under 3.14.8 is the study's own and has not been put to the owner.

n: 3.14
name: ice-water-gas-origin
kind: hub
is: The three words first appear on the disk in the first commit of the Living Codex, 2025-09-09: ice is essential persisted facts, water materialized caches, gas derivable or transient, with compiled code as gas. NUMS.Go has none of the words. The study counts 21 uses on 12 axes: 12 compatible, 5 conflicting, 4 loose. The owner rejected the binding of state to kind on 2026-06-08. No definition by the owner was found, only short statements. The study proposes state as the reach of a node's commitment, three invariants and six operations.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.1
name: origin
kind: hub
is: The oldest definition on the disk is the Living Codex of September 2025, committed under the owner's name with no assistant trailer: a state field on every node, ice kept small, the spec as ice and compiled code as gas, and code that refuses illegal moves. Its melt edits a node under the same id, and the older foundation document its spec cites is not on the disk.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.1.1
name: oldest-definition
kind: observation
