n: 3.14.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: The study's own proposal, found in no single source and not put to the owner: the state of a node is the reach of its commitment, independent of its kind; three checkable invariants (only water is mutable, a node references only nodes at least as committed, a transition conserves the node); ice marked essential or pinned, with essential ice kept small and compiled code never essential; six named operations of which only freeze needs an offer; counts and heat are readings that invite a move.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.1
name: state-is-reach-of-commitment
kind: finding
is: Proposal: the state of a node is the reach of its commitment, a property independent of the node's kind (blueprint, recipe or cell). It answers one question: who may rely on this node, and what is lost if it goes?
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.3.6 3.14.4.1
limit: A reconstruction by the study from short statements and one early design; the study says it should be put to the owner as a question, not adopted.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.2
name: three-states-defined
kind: finding
is: Proposal: gas is committed to no one, private to one evaluation or process, and nothing is lost if it goes. Water is committed to its holder, mutable by the holder only, and lives while the holder lives. Ice is committed to everyone, identified by its canonical bytes, never mutated, durable and shared by identity.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.4.1 3.14.3.4 3.14.3.5 3.14.2.8
limit: One earlier use gives gas little or no body (an identity barely instantiated), another a full node population in private RAM; the proposal allows both and leaves open whether another node may address a gas node. Water folds a read-only cache and a mutable draft into one state.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.3
name: only-water-is-mutable
kind: finding
is: Proposed invariant 1: among nodes with a reader other than their maker, only water is mutable, and only by its holder. Ice is never written after birth. Gas has no reader but its maker and may change freely.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.8.2
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.4
name: reference-only-as-committed
kind: finding
is: Proposed invariant 2: a node references only nodes at least as committed as itself. Ice points only at ice, so its identity is computable and means the same everywhere; water points at water and ice; gas at anything. The Living Codex edge rule and the frozen file of the 2026-11-05 carrier already follow this rule.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.1.4 3.14.2.9 1.3
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.5
name: transition-conserves-the-node
kind: finding
is: Proposed invariant 3: a transition conserves the node and never changes its kind. A transition changes where the body is held and who may rely on it. With identity computed from content, the identity is conserved only while the content is unchanged.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.3.2 3.14.3.3 1.3
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.6
name: essential-and-pinned-ice
kind: finding
is: Proposal: ice carries one of two marks. Essential ice has no recorded deriving recipe and its loss is real; pinned ice is a kept result whose deriving recipe and inputs are ice. The rule to keep ice small applies to essential ice. Compiled machine code is never essential: it is gas (a page in RAM) or water (a keyed cache), at most pinned.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.1.2 3.14.1.3 3.14.2.7 3.14.3.1
limit: Whether a derivable artifact may be ice at all is open: the Living Codex audit demotes regenerable nodes to water, while the cache file of 2026-06-17 pins them as ice. The pinned mark is the study's bridge between the two.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.7
name: six-named-operations
kind: finding
is: Proposed operations: condense (gas to water) materializes a body; freeze (water to ice) computes the identity and checks every child is ice; melt (ice to water) opens a mutable copy and leaves the ice as it is; evaporate (water to gas) releases the body; sublimate (ice to gas) drops the bytes and keeps the identity; thaw reads ice and verifies it.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.1.4 3.14.2.3 3.14.2.4 3.14.2.7 3.14.2.9 3.14.3.2
limit: The name evaporate is taken from the 2026-02 specs, where it meant loading into the runtime. A direct move from gas to ice is condense followed by freeze and gets no name.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.8.8
name: freeze-is-offered-readings-invite
kind: finding
is: Proposal: freeze is the one transition that needs an offer, because it creates something others will rely on; the holder offers and the store acknowledges. Sublimate is refused for essential ice that is referenced. Counts and heat are readings that invite a freeze, a melt, a sublimate or a pin; a reading performs nothing.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 1.5 3.14.1.2 3.14.2.4 3.14.3.2
limit: Which of the four acknowledgments a freeze returns was not examined. Whether unreferenced essential ice may lose its bytes without consent is not settled.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.9
name: drop
kind: hub
is: Five uses the study's proposal leaves out: state bound to kind, which the owner rejected; the word ice for compiled code, compiled images and compile tiers; the application's idea lifecycle and queue pressure as states of a node; plasma as a fourth state; and a melt that edits a node under the same id.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.9.1
name: kind-as-state
kind: finding
is: Drop the binding Blueprint = ice, Recipe = water, NamedCell = gas. The owner rejected it on 2026-06-08 and a later commit under the owner's identity calls it "The misunderstanding". Any kind of node may be in any state.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.14.2.2 3.14.3.3 3.14.4.2
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.9.2
name: ice-for-compiled-code
kind: finding
is: Drop the word ice for compiled native code, on-disk compiled images and compile tiers; in the proposal these are pinned or cached materializations. The round-one mapping of compile tiers (stored node form as ice, baseline code as water, speculative code as gas) is a new axis that no owner statement supports.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.4.3 3.14.2.6 3.14.8.6
limit: The four round-one mappings were written without the sources this study read; two of them land on the compatible reading.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.9.3
name: lifecycle-and-queue-words
kind: finding
is: Leave out of the definition of node state the application's idea lifecycle, where ice means "not yet implemented" and water comes after ice, and queue pressure, where ice means a full queue. They measure other things: how far an idea is built, and how full a queue is. The lifecycle runs gas, ice, water, an order the node states do not have, and the application applies it to every node of its own graph; the queue reading uses the node states' own codes 0, 1 and 2. The application may keep its own words.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.2.3 3.14.2.10
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.9.4
name: plasma-as-state
kind: finding
is: Drop plasma as a fourth state. It was added on 2026-08-14 in a commit with no trailer, and no owner statement was found for it. In the proposal a node that is both widely read and fast-changing is described by a reading, not by a state.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.14.2.10 3.14.3.6
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin

n: 3.14.9.5
name: melt-that-keeps-the-id
kind: finding
is: Drop the 2025 melt's mutation in place, which leaves no ice behind. In the 2025 code the id is an assigned string and the content hash a separate field, so that melt already keeps continuity on a name while content changes; it does not conflict with content addressing. The proposal's melt opens a working copy that remembers the ice it came from, and continuity moves to the name that is re-bound after a later freeze.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.14.1.5 1.3
limit: Moving continuity to the name binding is not attested by the owner.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-ice-water-gas-origin
